# PART 11 — RECENT JOB EXAM TREND INTELLIGENCE

This is another major product feature.

The platform must analyze recent job examination questions and identify which topics have appeared in those examinations.

Then it must match those topics against the user's uploaded books and generate relevant practice questions.

Suggested feature name:

Recent Exam Trend Intelligence

## 11.1 Examination Categories

The system should support categories such as:

- BCS
- Government Bank Recruitment
- Private Bank Recruitment
- Primary Teacher Recruitment
- NTRCA and Teacher Recruitment
- Ministry Recruitment
- Department and Directorate Recruitment
- Autonomous Institutions
- Other Competitive Job Examinations

The category list must be configurable and extensible.

## 11.2 Examination Data Sources

The system may use:

1. User-uploaded previous examination question papers.
2. Reliable online sources and official publications where available.
3. Manually entered examination questions and topic information.

Every analyzed examination must maintain:

- Examination Name
- Organization
- Examination Date
- Source
- Source URL, if available
- Question Paper File Reference, if uploaded
- Analysis Status
- Topic List
- Confidence Level
- Verification Status

Never fabricate recent examination questions, dates, or sources.

If no verified question paper is available, clearly state that the analysis is incomplete.

## 11.3 Topic Identification

AI should identify:

- Subject
- Topic
- Subtopic
- Question Type
- Difficulty
- Knowledge Area
- Related Book Chapter

Example:

Bangla:
- Samas
- Sandhi
- Idioms
- Grammar

English:
- Tense
- Voice
- Preposition
- Vocabulary

Mathematics:
- Percentage
- Ratio
- Profit and Loss
- Time and Work

General Knowledge:
- Bangladesh Constitution
- Liberation War
- Geography
- International Affairs

ICT:
- Number System
- Networking
- Computer Fundamentals

These are examples, not a fixed or exhaustive list.

## 11.4 Matching With Uploaded Books

After identifying topics:

- Search Shared Book Library and authorized Personal Books.
- Identify books and chapters covering those topics.
- Match extracted content to identified topics.
- Show which topics are available and which are missing.
- Do not generate book-based questions from content that does not exist in the selected books.
- Keep source references for generated questions.

## 11.5 Trend-Based Question Generation

Generate new practice questions using:

- Recent examination topics.
- Uploaded book content.
- Relevant chapter information.
- Previous examination question patterns.
- Selected difficulty and question types.

Do not copy previous examination questions wholesale.

The objective is to create new questions that test similar knowledge and skills.

## 11.6 Time Range and Topic Distribution

The user should be able to select a trend analysis period, such as:

- Last 6 months
- Last 1 year
- Last 2 years
- Custom date range

The system should also support filtering by examination category and organization.

Proposed default distribution:

- 70% questions from high-priority recent exam topics.
- 30% questions from other important related topics in uploaded books.

This is a configurable starting recommendation, NOT a permanent fixed rule.

The user must be able to change the distribution.

The system must explain that historical topic frequency does not guarantee future examination questions.

## 11.7 Trend Dashboard

Create a dashboard showing:

- Analyzed examinations.
- Exam dates.
- Source verification status.
- Topic frequency.
- Subject-wise distribution.
- Frequently repeated topics.
- High-priority topics.
- Available uploaded-book matches.
- Missing topics.
- Generated question sets.
- Trend-based mock tests.

Never present unverified estimates as factual statistics.

